Phase 1 vendoring manifest
--------------------------

Copied without edits:

* basetrack.py
* utils/__init__.py
* utils/kalman_filter.py
* utils/stracks.py

Local edits, marked with ``# LOCAL-EDIT`` where they occur:

* byte_tracker.py redirects the Ultralytics LOGGER and xywh2ltwh imports to
  compat.py.
* utils/matching.py removes the lap import and import-time package installer,
  removes the unused use_lap argument and solve-then-filter branch, redirects
  axis-aligned IoU and assignment to compat.py, and removes the torch-only OBB
  probability-IoU branch.
* trackers/__init__.py is reduced to the Phase 1 BYTETracker export so it does
  not import non-vendored or torch-dependent modules.

New compatibility file:

* compat.py contains NumPy-only copies of xywh2ltwh, xyxy2ltwh, and bbox_ioa
  from the same Ultralytics revision, plus a local logging object and a
  SciPy-backed replacement for lap.lapjv(extend_cost=True, cost_limit=...).
  The replacement uses lap's extended-matrix construction. Equal-objective
  assignment ties may resolve differently.
